    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick, mini.extra\n\n### Description\n\n### Current\nStarting a picker for workspace symbols does not require a query and can be nil, however if a query is not provided there are issues with LSPs like gopls where it requires a query before the picker allows you to filter through the items. If you don't provide a query the picker responds with: \"No symbols found.\" A dynamic picker that requeries within the picker without having to restart the picker might be one solution to this when working with LSPs like gopls.\n\n### Scenario\n1. Set CWD to a go project\n2. Run picker from a buffer inside that workspace without providing a query\n3. Feedback: \"No symbols found\"\n\n### Request\nComing from telescope I was using the dynamic workspace symbol picker which seems to requery when you type inside the picker. I have done a little digging around in the mini.extra module and it doesn't seem to have any out of the box solutions for dynamically updating the query after the picker has been started. I believe this is a feature that is needed for a true workspace symbol finder with LSPs like gopls. \n\n### Neovim version\n0.11.5",
