            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nAs [noted in the documentation](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/f43357be022565d969795cde29b8988d082cc913/doc/mini-extra.txt#L643), sending empty query (which is default) should result into all symbols shown according to the LSP specification. Here is the [relevant part of the LSP spec](https://microsoft.github.io/language-server-protocol/specifications/lsp/3.17/specification/#workspaceSymbolParams): \"... Clients may send an empty string here to request all symbols.\".\n\nThe problem is, the `gopls` here is intentionally not following LSP specification. It was reported in golang/go#47655 and was not ruled out as something that needs fixing.\n\nIn general, I don't think it is reasonable to adjust 'mini.extra' functionality for LSP servers that doesn't follow the specification.\n\n**That said**, something like `workspace_symbol_live` scope can be implemented within about 20 new lines (not including docs). And might indeed be reasonable (although I was not really convinced before starting to right this issue). I'll take a look.",
