            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This should now be resolved on latest `main`. Start it like `:Pick lsp scope='workspace_symbol_live'` and use it similarly to a `:Pick grep_live`.\n\n---\n\nNote for future. Although having this as a custom picker is possible, there were several reasons against it:\n- The `vim.lsp.buf.workspace_symbol('', { on_list = function() ... end })` doesn't even use `on_list` if there is no returned items. Instead it forces the \"No symbols found\" notification. This is exactly the case here. This is related to [this PR and comment](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/25830#issuecomment-1786006405). Probably a good idea to always force `on_list` route if it is supplied, but there will be endless discussions about whether it is the right choice (and whether `on_list` should be renamed then).\n- Manually working around [custom highlighting logic](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/dce9bc4e19d02d5c37fe71c16f40f8a5536b0386/lua/mini/extra.lua#L1953-L1959) is doable, but verbose.\n\nAs after a (reasonable) refactor the new scope only adds about 12 new lines of code, this seems fine to add as built-in.",
